From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 01:22:47 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] virt: gunyah: Report a missing resource manager log as
 information

Firmware without a resource manager log answers the log query with
"not supported", and the driver then logs "Error in returning log: -95"
at error level every time the module loads, although nothing failed:
the log is optional and the driver carries on without it.

Log that case at info level; other errors keep the error message.

Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/virt/gunyah/rsc_mgr.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/virt/gunyah/rsc_mgr.c b/drivers/virt/gunyah/rsc_mgr.c
index 9aacd013df20..7d7a5b569390 100644
--- a/drivers/virt/gunyah/rsc_mgr.c
+++ b/drivers/virt/gunyah/rsc_mgr.c
@@ -780,7 +780,11 @@ static int gunyah_rm_sysfs_register(struct gunyah_rm *rm)
 	int ret = gunyah_rm_get_log(rm, 0, &addr, &size);
 
 	if (ret < 0) {
-		pr_err("Error in returning log: %d\n", ret);
+		/* firmware without a resource manager log answers "not supported" */
+		if (ret == -EOPNOTSUPP)
+			pr_info("Resource manager log not available\n");
+		else
+			pr_err("Error in returning log: %d\n", ret);
 		return 0;
 	}
 
